This crate is a fork of luaux 0.2.0 (crates.io, revision dad67d6), part of
luau-xml, published under the MIT license. Alloy carries it as a path
dependency with three patches:

- `Config.extra_bound`: names the caller knows are bound, so a component
  declared with Alloy syntax resolves. Alloy's parser supplies them.
- `can_end_expression` counts `!`, so a comparison after a non-nil assert
  does not open markup.
- `compile::markup_spans` is public, so Alloy can blank markup before it
  collects bindings.

Every other line is upstream luaux. Upstream fixes land here by re-applying
the patches on the new revision.
